2.7. IoT System Design
The Arduino Mega 2560 reads data from sensors and sends this data via the Serial Port to the ESP8266. The ESP-8266 reads data from the Arduino Mega 2560 through the Serial Port to compute the average values and then transmits the data to Node-RED using the MQTT protocol. Node-RED on the server waits for data from the MQTT protocol, stores this data in the server's database, and allows a web application to retrieve and display the data from the server's database, as illustrated in Figure 4.


