3.2. Methane (CH4) Emissions
The methane emission (CH4) while feeding BSF larvae with food at different pH levels continuously increased over time. Initially, CH4 emissions fluctuated but then showed a general trend of increase. The highest CH4 emissions were observed for pH 8.0 (18.37 PPM on Day 4), pH 4.0 (17.87 PPM on Day 14), pH 10.0 (17.87 PPM on Day 6), pH 7.0 (17.47 PPM on Day 14), pH 2.0 (17.45 PPM on Day 14), and pH 6.0 (17.17 PPM on Day 5). Conversely, the lowest CH4 emissions were recorded for pH 8.0 (14.53 PPM on Day 1), pH 4.0 (14.69 PPM on Day 6), pH 10.0 (14.82 PPM on Day 1), pH 2.0 (14.97 PPM on Day 4), pH 6.0 (15.64 PPM on Day 3), and pH 7.0 (15.87 PPM on Day 9).
